{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LHcCHNeuDQDkA6yqFZBr2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Working tree is clean and all work is committed. The `execute-todo` run is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAll ten SOS cards are implemented, tested through the real engine, and committed — one commit per card plus one for the shared engine seams. Final state: **1244 tests passing** (1145 engine regression + 60 SOS + 39 FDN), `engine_tests/` never regressed, all ten card classes import cleanly.\n\n**Shared engine seams (built first, reused widely):**\n- **E1** — fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell` (drives casualty, animated-land pump)\n- **E2** — `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` fired from `advance_phase` after emptying pools (delayed/recurring main-phase triggers)\n- **E3** — battlefield cost-reduction aggregation in `get_cost_reduction` (granted affinity)\n\n**The ten cards:**\n| Card | Key mechanic | \n|---|---|\n| sos_4 Together as One | Converge via `colors_spent` |\n| sos_1 The Dawning Archaic | cost reduction + attack-trigger free-cast + exile-instead |\n| sos_245 Witherbloom | self-affinity + granted affinity (E3) |\n| sos_226 Silverquill | granted Casualty 1 (E1 + `copy_spell`) |\n| sos_257 Great Hall | restricted mana + {5} in-place animation + pump |\n| sos_57 Mana Sculpt | counter + delayed `{C}` refund (E2) |\n| sos_120 Improvisation Capstone | cast-from-exile + Paradigm recurring copy (E2) |\n| sos_13 Emeritus // Swords | ETB token + Prepared + cast-from-exile |\n| sos_201 Lorehold | card-local miracle + opponent-upkeep loot |\n| sos_97 Ral Zarek | planeswalker: surveil / discard / reanimate / coin-flip skip-turns |\n\n**Engine changes were all additive and minimal** — no renames/moves/deletes. Beyond E1–E3: fired `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (never fired before), added `SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent` so spells can be exiled on resolution, `ManaPool` restricted-mana tracking, `card.mana_spent` storage, loyalty-ability targets, `game.rng`, and `Player.skip_turns` with turn-skip handling. Each deliberate limitation and ambiguous-clause ruling is logged in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\nOne notable finding logged along the way: the engine fires a permanent's ETB event *before* calling its `register_triggers`, so a self-\"when this enters\" trigger must be registered in `on_cast` (verified empirically) — this is how sos_13's ETB works."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":386825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":604},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fef623c-942b-4e62-9572-a5757d885aba","uuid":"c52c2efe-a207-4982-af06-6052620cfed0","request_id":"req_011Cbvgt1GmuAtTmYtSFvkr5"}
